Async Alembic migrations for {{ cookiecutter.project_name }}.

Alembic is the source of schema truth for every deployed environment. The
option-aware initial revision creates every table shipped by this generated
project. The local environment may instead auto-create tables at startup
(DB_AUTO_CREATE, on by default only when ENVIRONMENT=local); staging and
production must apply schema with `alembic upgrade head`{% if cookiecutter.use_docker == "yes" %} — the compose api service runs it on boot{% endif %}.

Create a new revision after changing models:
    make revision m="describe your change"

Apply migrations:
    make migrate

Roll back the most recent migration:
    make downgrade

Generating later revisions
--------------------------
Autogenerate diffs the models against a live database, so it must run against
a database containing ONLY what earlier migrations created. Tables auto-created
by DB_AUTO_CREATE can make autogenerate miss changes. To generate a later
revision cleanly:
{% if cookiecutter.use_docker == "yes" %}
    docker compose down -v   # discard the auto-created local schema
    make db-up
    make migrate             # bring the fresh database up to head
    make revision m="describe the model change"
{%- else %}
    1. Point DATABASE_URL at an empty database.
    2. make migrate          # bring it up to head
    3. make revision m="describe the model change"
{%- endif %}

When you add a new domain, import its models module in migrations/env.py so
its tables register on the metadata autogenerate compares against.
